            devotionalText: "Jesus didn't just teach obedience — He lived it to the ultimate degree. He obeyed the Father all the way to the cross. His obedience cost Him everything. When you struggle with obedience, look at Jesus. He understands the cost. He walked the hardest road of obedience ever walked. And He walks with you in yours.",
            prayerText: "Jesus, Your obedience went all the way to the cross. Mine feels small in comparison, yet You understand my struggle. Give me the same spirit of humble obedience. Help me say 'not my will, but Yours' even when obedience costs me. I follow Your example today. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What is the hardest act of obedience God has asked of you? How does Jesus' example encourage you?",
            actionSteps: ["Read Philippians 2:1-11 and meditate on Christ's obedience", "Do one thing today that costs you something as an act of obedience"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Deuteronomy 30:19-20",
            scriptureText: "This day I call the heavens and the earth as witnesses against you that I have set before you life and death, blessings and curses. Now choose life, so that you and your children may live and that you may love the Lord your God, listen to his voice, and hold fast to him.",
            devotionalTitle: "Obedience Is a Choice",
            devotionalText: "God sets two paths before you every day: life and death, blessing and curse. And then He tells you which to choose. Obedience isn't something that happens to you — it's a daily, deliberate choice. Each decision is a fork in the road. Choose life. Choose obedience. The blessing is on the other side of the right choice.",
            prayerText: "Lord, today I choose life. I choose obedience. I choose blessing. Help me see every decision as a choice between Your way and my own. Give me the strength to consistently choose Your path. I want my choices to bring life — to me and to those who come after me. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What choice are you facing today where obedience would mean choosing life?",
            actionSteps: ["At your next decision point today, pause and consciously choose God's way", "Write 'Choose life' on your mirror or phone and let it guide your decisions"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "John 13:17",
            scriptureText: "Now that you know these things, you will be blessed if you do them.",
            devotionalTitle: "Blessing Follows Doing",
            devotionalText: "Jesus says the blessing isn't in the knowing — it's in the doing. You can know everything about God's will and miss the blessing entirely if you don't act. The gap between knowing and doing is where most Christians get stuck. Bridge that gap today. Do what you know. The blessing is waiting on the other side of action.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I know many things about Your will. Help me move from knowing to doing. Close the gap between what I understand and how I live. I don't want to be blessed in theory — I want to be blessed in practice. Give me the courage to act on what I know. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What is one thing you know God wants you to do that you haven't done yet?",
            actionSteps: ["Bridge the knowing-doing gap: act on one truth you already know today", "Ask a friend to hold you accountable for following through on what God has shown you"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Acts 5:29",
            scriptureText: "Peter and the other apostles replied: 'We must obey God rather than human beings!'",
            devotionalTitle: "When Obedience Gets Costly",
            devotionalText: "The apostles were threatened with punishment for preaching about Jesus. Their response was clear: God's authority trumps human authority. Sometimes obeying God means going against the crowd, risking relationships, or facing consequences. Obedience isn't always comfortable or popular. But when God and culture conflict, the choice is clear: obey God.",
            prayerText: "Lord, give me the courage to obey You even when it costs me. When following You goes against the crowd, help me stand firm. I want to be more concerned with Your approval than anyone else's. Give me the boldness of the apostles. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Is there an area where obeying God would put you at odds with the people around you?",
            actionSteps: ["Identify one area where cultural pressure conflicts with God's commands and choose God's way", "Pray for boldness to obey God in situations where it's unpopular"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Matthew 7:24-25",
            scriptureText: "Therefore everyone who hears these words of mine and puts them into practice is like a wise man who built his house on the rock. The rain came down, the streams rose, and the winds blew and beat against that house; yet it did not fall, because it had its foundation on the rock.",
            devotionalTitle: "Build on the Rock",
            devotionalText: "Jesus says the difference between a life that stands and one that collapses isn't hearing — both builders heard. It's practice. Putting God's words into action builds a foundation that storms can't shake. Disobedience is like building on sand — it looks fine until the storm hits. Obedience builds something that lasts.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I want to build my life on the rock of obedience. Help me not just hear Your words but practice them. When storms come — and they will — I want to stand firm because I've built on a solid foundation. Make me a doer, not just a hearer. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Is your life built on the rock of obedience or the sand of good intentions?",
            actionSteps: ["Put one of Jesus' teachings into practice today — choose something specific from the Sermon on the Mount", "Ask yourself: 'If a storm hit my life today, what would my foundation look like?'"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Psalm 119:105",
            scriptureText: "Your word is a lamp for my feet, a light on my path.",
            devotionalTitle: "One Step at a Time",
            devotionalText: "A lamp doesn't illuminate the whole road — just the next step. God's Word works the same way. You don't need to see the whole journey to obey today's instruction. Obedience is often one step at a time, one day at a time, one decision at a time. Don't wait for full clarity. Obey the light you have, and more light will come.",
            prayerText: "Lord, Your Word lights my next step. I don't need to see the whole path — just enough to obey today. Help me be faithful with the light I have. As I obey what I can see, reveal what's ahead. I trust You one step at a time. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Are you waiting for full clarity before you obey, or walking in the light you already have?",
            actionSteps: ["Obey the clearest instruction God has given you, even if you can't see what comes next", "Read one psalm today and act on whatever instruction it gives"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Hebrews 5:8",
            scriptureText: "Son though he was, he learned obedience from what he suffered.",
            devotionalTitle: "Obedience Learned Through Difficulty",
            devotionalText: "Even Jesus learned obedience through suffering. Not because He was disobedient, but because obedience is a muscle that strengthens under pressure. Easy circumstances don't teach you much about obedience. Difficulty does. When obeying God is hard — that's when your obedience becomes real, tested, and strong.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I don't enjoy the difficult parts of obedience, but I trust that they're making me stronger. Help me learn from the hard moments instead of running from them. If Jesus learned obedience through suffering, I can learn it through my challenges. Strengthen my obedience in the fire. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What has difficulty taught you about obedience that ease never could?",
            actionSteps: ["Identify a hard situation you're in and ask 'What is God teaching me about obedience here?'", "Thank God for one difficulty that strengthened your faith"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Isaiah 1:19",
            scriptureText: "If you are willing and obedient, you will eat the good of the land.",
            devotionalTitle: "Willing and Obedient",
            devotionalText: "God pairs two words: willing and obedient. You can obey grudgingly or willingly. God wants both your compliance and your heart. A willing heart transforms obedience from duty to delight. Don't just obey — be willing. The promise is clear: the good of the land is waiting for those who bring both their will and their actions.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I want to be both willing and obedient — not one without the other. Where my heart resists, soften it. Where my actions lag, strengthen them. I choose to obey with a willing spirit. The good of the land is ahead, and I walk toward it with an eager heart. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Are you obeying God willingly or reluctantly? What would change if your heart matched your actions?",
            actionSteps: ["Do one act of obedience today with genuine willingness, not grudging compliance", "Ask God to change your heart about an area where you obey reluctantly"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Luke 5:4-6",
            scriptureText: "When he had finished speaking, he said to Simon, 'Put out into deep water, and let down the nets for a catch.' Simon answered, 'Master, we've worked hard all night and haven't caught anything. But because you say so, I will let down the nets.' When they had done so, they caught such a large number of fish that their nets began to break.",
            devotionalTitle: "Because You Say So",
            devotionalText: "Peter had every reason not to obey. He was tired. He'd fished all night. Nothing was biting. His experience said it was pointless. But he obeyed anyway: 'Because you say so.' And the result was nets breaking with abundance. Sometimes God's commands don't match your experience. Obey anyway. 'Because You say so' might be the most powerful prayer of obedience you ever pray.",
            prayerText: "Lord, even when my experience says otherwise, I choose to obey because You say so. My logic might resist, my tiredness might complain, but Your word is enough. I let down my nets at Your command and trust You for the catch. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Where is God asking you to do something that doesn't make sense based on your experience?",
            actionSteps: ["Obey one prompting from God today even if your experience says it won't work", "Pray 'because You say so, Lord' before acting on God's instruction"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Romans 6:16",
            scriptureText: "Don't you know that when you offer yourselves to someone as obedient slaves, you are slaves of the one you obey — whether you are slaves to sin, which leads to death, or to obedience, which leads to righteousness?",
            devotionalTitle: "Everyone Obeys Something",
            devotionalText: "You're always obeying something — either sin or God. There's no neutral ground. Every choice moves you toward death or righteousness. The question isn't whether you'll obey. It's what you'll obey. Choose wisely. Obedience to God leads to righteousness and life. Obedience to sin leads to destruction.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I choose to offer myself to You as an obedient servant. I don't want to be enslaved to sin's commands. I want to follow Your voice, which leads to righteousness and life. Help me recognize when I'm obeying sin and redirect my steps toward You. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "What are you obeying in the areas of your life where you're not obeying God?",
            actionSteps: ["Identify one habit where you're obeying sin instead of God and take a step away from it", "Replace one sinful pattern with an act of obedience to God today"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "2 John 1:6",
            scriptureText: "And this is love: that we walk in obedience to his commands. As you have heard from the beginning, his command is that you walk in love.",
            devotionalTitle: "Love and Obedience in a Circle",
            devotionalText: "John creates a beautiful circle: love is walking in obedience, and God's command is to walk in love. Obedience and love feed each other. The more you obey, the more you love. The more you love, the more naturally you obey. They're not separate tracks — they're the same path. Walk in love. Walk in obedience. It's one walk.",
            prayerText: "Lord, help me see that love and obedience are the same walk. As I obey You, deepen my love. As my love grows, make obedience more natural. I don't want to separate what You've joined together. I walk in love and obedience today — one path, one heart. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "How has your love for God grown as a result of your obedience? How has obedience grown from your love?",
            actionSteps: ["Do one loving thing for someone today as an act of obedience to God's command", "Reflect on how love and obedience have strengthened each other in your life"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Jonah 1:3",
            scriptureText: "But Jonah ran away from the Lord and headed for Tarshish.",
            devotionalTitle: "The Cost of Running",
            devotionalText: "Jonah heard God clearly and ran the opposite direction. Disobedience always takes you somewhere — but never where you want to go. Jonah ended up in a storm, in the sea, and in a fish. Running from God is exhausting, costly, and ultimately futile. He's patient enough to wait and persistent enough to pursue. You might as well obey now and save yourself the whale.",
            prayerText: "Lord, I stop running. Wherever I've been heading in the opposite direction of Your will, I turn around. Forgive my disobedience. I don't want to learn lessons the hard way. I choose Your direction over my own. No more running. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Is there an area where you've been running from what God has asked you to do?",
            actionSteps: ["Identify your 'Tarshish' — the direction you run when God calls — and turn around", "Read Jonah 1-2 and notice the cost of disobedience and the grace in God's pursuit"]
        ),
        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "Matthew 28:19-20",
            scriptureText: "Therefore go and make disciples of all nations, baptizing them in the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, and teaching them to obey everything I have commanded you.",
            devotionalTitle: "Teach Others to Obey",
            devotionalText: "The Great Commission isn't just about sharing the gospel — it's about teaching people to obey everything Jesus commanded. Discipleship is teaching obedience. Your obedience isn't just for you — it becomes the model for those watching. When you obey well, you teach others how to follow Jesus. Your life is a classroom.",
            prayerText: "Lord, help me obey so well that others can learn by watching me. I want my life to be a discipleship classroom where obedience is taught by example. Use my faithfulness to inspire others to follow You. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "Who is learning about obedience by watching your life?",
            actionSteps: ["Mentor one person this week by sharing something God taught you through obedience", "Ask yourself: 'Would someone learn good obedience by following my example?'"]
