        DayContent(
            scriptureReference: "John 15:10-11",
            scriptureText: "If you keep my commands, you will remain in my abide in my love, just as I have kept my Father's commands and remain in his love. I have told you this so that my joy may be in you and your joy may be complete.",
            devotionalTitle: "Obedience Leads to Joy",
            devotionalText: "Jesus connects obedience to two things: abiding in His love and complete joy. Obedience doesn't drain you — it fills you. It keeps you in the place where God's love is most experienced and where joy is most complete. Disobedience might feel like freedom, but it leads to emptiness. Obedience is the path to the fullest joy you can experience.",
            prayerText: "Jesus, I want to remain in Your love and experience complete joy. Help me see obedience as the path to fullness, not restriction. I keep Your commands not to earn Your love, but to stay in the place where I experience it most. Fill me with Your joy through my obedience today. In Jesus' name, amen.",
            reflectionPrompt: "When has obedience led to unexpected joy in your life?",
            actionSteps: ["Obey one of Jesus' commands today and pay attention to the joy that follows", "Journal about a time when obedience brought you deeper into God's love"]
        ),
